-   entry .Fit   a histogram's fit: the bin `#edges`, the abscissa over them and the ordinate of counts
-     entry #edges   the bin edges, one more than the bins, at round steps
-     entry #abscissa   the linear `Scale` from the first edge to the last
-     entry #ordinate   the `Scale` of counts, from zero to the most-counted bin, padded to a round step
-   entry .Style   the same components as `Bars.Style`: a histogram draws bars
-   entry .samples   one sample set is plottable as a histogram
-   entry .traversable   any collection traversable by sample sets is plottable as a histogram
-   entry #bins   the number of bins, or `Unset` for Sturges' rule
-   entry #ordinate   a calibration for the ordinate of counts, or `Unset` for linear
+   entry .Fit   o ajuste de um histograma: os `#edges` das classes, a abscissa sobre eles e a ordenada das contagens
+     entry #edges   os limites das classes, um a mais que as classes, em passos redondos
+     entry #abscissa   a `Scale` linear do primeiro limite ao último
+     entry #ordinate   a `Scale` das contagens, do zero até a classe mais contada, arredondada até um passo redondo
+   entry .Style   os mesmos componentes de `Bars.Style`: um histograma desenha barras
